{
  "info": {
    "name": "Relay Chat API (Socket.IO + REST)",
    "description": "REST API of the real-time chat app. Start the server (`npm run dev`), seed the demo data (`npm run seed`), then run **Auth → Login (demo: Lina)** first. It saves the tokens into collection variables, and every other request sends them as a Bearer token (set once on the collection's Authorization tab).\n\n- **Users → Contacts** saves another user's id as `{{otherUserId}}`\n- **Conversations → List / Open direct chat / Create group** save `{{conversationId}}`\n- **Conversations → List messages** saves the oldest loaded message as `{{oldestMessageId}}` for paging\n\nAccess tokens expire after JWT_EXPIRES_IN (10m): on 401 \"Invalid or expired token\", run **Auth → Refresh token**.\n\nEvery response uses the JSend shape `{ status: \"success\" | \"fail\" | \"error\", data | message }`.\n\n## Socket.IO (not in this file)\n\nPostman exports Socket.IO requests only inside a workspace, not in a v2.1 collection file, so create one by hand: **New → Socket.IO**.\n\n- URL: `http://localhost:3000` (the server root, not /api)\n- Headers: `Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}` (run a Login request first; the browser client uses the handshake `auth.token` instead)\n- Settings → Client version: v4\n- Listen to: `message:new`, `message:read`, `typing:start`, `typing:stop`, `presence:update`, `presence:snapshot`, `conversation:new`, `conversation:updated`, `conversation:removed`, `message:error`, `auth:expired`, `session:ended`\n- Emit (JSON, tick **Ack** to see the answer):\n  - `conversation:join` `{ \"conversationId\": \"{{conversationId}}\" }`\n  - `message:send` `{ \"conversationId\": \"{{conversationId}}\", \"text\": \"Hello from Postman\", \"clientId\": \"postman-0001\" }`\n  - `message:read` `{ \"conversationId\": \"{{conversationId}}\" }`\n  - `typing:start` / `typing:stop` `{ \"conversationId\": \"{{conversationId}}\" }` (after conversation:join)\n  - `conversation:leave` `{}`\n\nTip: sending through **Conversations → Send message (REST)** while a browser has the chat open shows the message arrive live, because the REST route broadcasts `message:new` too.\n\nFull event reference: docs/SOCKET_EVENTS.md",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{accessToken}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
